        "text": "There is a town, where grew a young man, who walked a graveled dead end road.\nAt the end, there stood a mountain, where ran a river made of snow\nBeside this mountain, there stands a wood stool, where sits a young man who calls it home\nNothing in hand, foot prints behind him, thought, and silence, all alone\n \nIn this town, there grew a young girl, who walked a graveled dead end road.\nAt the end, there stood a wood stool, where sat a young man no one knows.\nFor the day, she stood beside him, just to remind him he's not alone\nThe young man smiled, broke his silence, took her hand and walked her home.\n \nThere is a day, that finds all young men, when time surrounds them, and paths are shown\nWalking back, the day had found him, below this mountain he had grown\nNo questions asked, he packed his wood stool, and started climbing in the snow\nLeaving behind, two sets of footprints, some that ended, and some his own.\n \nNow there's a town, where sits a cabin, that sleeps a young girl who calls it home\nWhen she wakes, she sees a mountain, where runs a river made of snow\nEach day she walks, and seeks a young man, who had a wood stool he called his own\nForever lost, along that dirt road, paved in gravel all alone.\n \nThere is a day, that finds all young girls, when time surrounds them, and paths are shown\nWalking one day, that time had found her, on this dirt road she had grown\nNo questions asked, she left the small town, and started climbing in the snow\nLeaving behind, one set of footprints, the road had ended, and two where shown.\n \nThere is a place, along that river where sits an oak tree in the snow\nIn this tree, is carved a message, from a grown man no one knows\nThese words are there, and sit forever, in the oak tree as it grows\nIf your here, please sit beside me, when the sun sets Ill walk you home\n \nFor years she climbed, that lonely mountain, until she found him in the snow\nBy a tree, that read a message, there died a young man she had known\nFrom that tree, she built a cabin on a mountain where no one goes\nWithin its walls, she placed a wood stool, where sat a grown man she called her own\n \nThe sun went down, there stood a spirit, who paved a new road made of stone\nThe new road shined, and wrapped the mountain, along a river made of snow\nfor days they walked, along that river, until they found a dead end road\nLeaving behind, two sets of footprints, some that ended, and some her own.\n \nThere is a place, where sits a mountain, and runs a river made of snow.\nThere is a road, that winds the river, and wraps the mountain where no one goes.\nBelow a ledge, that peeks the mountain, there sits a cabin made of oak.\nWithin its walls, there reads a message, and stands a wood stool called my home. \n  "
