        "text": "Revolution, what is it to you?\nSubstitution, for nothing new.\nNo resolution, just repeating things we knew.\nRevolution, is nothing new.\n \nYou hear it every day, people change but nothings changed,\nSatisfied by a clockwork tide, that we ride from day to day.\nThe same things re-arranged, fallow shame with endless shame,\nHide the lies in a sea of lives, that strive to stay the same.\n \nWill we always be at war? Is it ever worth not fighting for?\nFoolish pride, and lust struck lives stuck inside revolving doors.\nMust we always let our bullets sore? As body bags line up the shore,\nEvery day we must learn once more, bloodshed is not a settled score.\n \nEverybody likes to pretend, that all is fair and nothing ends,\nChildren hold the key to a better world, but nobody invites them in.\nTaught to walk before they swim, made to mimic last years trend,\nIdeas tied on their brilliant minds, despite what might have worked for them.\n \nRevolution, what is it to you?\nSubstitution, for nothing new.\nNo resolution, just repeating things we knew.\nRevolution, is nothing new.\nAuthor notes\nRevolution rev·o·lu·tion/ˌrevəˈlo͞oSHən/\nNoun: a procedure or course, as if in a circuit, back to a starting point.\n  "
