        "title": "Sad Song",
        "date": "August 26, 2009",
        "text": "Tattooed tears fall like rain on my face today.\nPermanent reminders of my sins.\nFrom blue eyes they fall again, painting the way.\nUntil my eyes run dry, and the blue turns to gray.\nAll of the pain within released with a blade.\nThe cut runs so deep and then.\nThe blood joins the tears in a sweet serenade.\nSinging my soul to sleep night after night\nHoping the next cut bleeds me tearless and dry.\nAnd I dance to this sad song,\nright up till dawn.\nDeath will be coming, before too long.\nThe cut all but kills me,\nthe scar still remains.\nHundreds of white lines,\nand all have their names.\nLying, cheating, yelling, screaming.\nall carved so deeply, into my veins.\nThrough the night they remind me of the reason I cry,\nAnd they all join together to sing this lullaby.\nAnd I dance to this sad song,\nRight up till dawn.\nDeath will be coming before too long\nDepression becomes me.\nAll light fades away.\nFalling so deeply in love with the pain.\nAgain and again the marks grow on my veins.\nDeath wont come quick enough so one choice remains.\nSo I stand in my room and I pick up the gun.\nThis is it, the end, it cannot be undone.\nThe barrel it sings to me,\nit seems to be fun.\nmy scars blood and tears join in all in one.\nAnd I dance to this sad song,\nright up till dawn.\nDeath will be coming before too long.\nAnd I die to this sad song,\nthey find me at dawn.\nMaybe here is where I belong."
