        "text": "Drivin down my block the side walk is packed with empty blue eyes\nthe dried chalk, that white chalk, under every tall building it lies\nI cant talk my jaws locked the devil is here in disguise\nI'm hearin tic toc the clock stopped to watch a young boy as he cry's \n \nMake it go away\nI don't wanna stay here\nthere's nothin else to say here\nmake it go away\n \nmother I'm afraid\nI don't wanna play here\nI just wanna lay here\nand make it go away\n \nwhile he walks home the cold stone burns his bare feet every stride\nAt a slow roam he's all alone no one would care if he died\nPassin by the drug home a harsh tone rings from a mans forty five\nunder grown and bare boned he dropped to one knee and he cried\n \nMake it go away\nI don't wanna stay here\nthere's nothin else to say here\nmake it go away\n \nmother I'm afraid\nI don't wanna play here\nI just wanna lay here\nand make it go away\n \nThe boy falls down with no sound as dead as the look in all eyes\nthe cold ground is red now but no one looks down to realize\nhe is never found just drawn around with chalk where he lies\nevery night the same sound the whole town lays down to sleep and it cries\n \nMake it go away\nI don't wanna stay here\nthere's nothin else to say here\nmake it go away\n \nmother I'm afraid\nI don't wanna play here\nI just wanna lay here\nand make it go away"
