        "title": "Windowsill",
        "date": "March 3, 2010",
        "text": "Sky Captain\n\nMarch 3, 2010.  © Talon Truitt Cherry, All rights reserved\nOn a pirates ship just south of Outskirts Toledo\nI sailed through the white clouds with old captain Grey\nSailed away through the sunset but who cares where we go\nCause we know the compass will show us the way\n \nHoist the sales, raise anchor, drink rum, laugh at danger\nThe sky captain's crew men can make no mistakes\nTake the time you spend here to release all that anger\nPrepare for the tide turn when new daylight breaks\n \nIt cracks like a pistol the day breaks like crystal\nThe whistle is sounded the ship shifts and shakes\nThis one isn't little we flew through the middle\nMother earth takes her toll on all our mistakes\n \nThree days from the harbor the storms getting harder\nIt seams that the kind stars have sealed all our fates\nGrey's face shows no bother the old captain's smarter\nHe charters a new course and measures the stakes\n \nHoist the sales, raise your glasses, yell loud bet your asses\nThe sky captain's crew men will make no mistake\nStill mother earth thrashes our ship as she crashes\nThe sky captain's crew men were no match for her wake\n \nYou once told me you could save time in bottle\nAnd coddle the memories fleeing each day\nCould I have just a small sip, hardly a swallow\nAnd bring back the memories with old captain Grey"
